WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.270
- Social media is like a slot machine,

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:03.980
pull the lever and you
may hit the jackpot,

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:04.880
or you may get zilch,

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:06.140
which is usually what happens.

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.700
But with me, you always
win big 'cause I'm amazing.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:09.722
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:09.722 --> 00:00:11.946
(upbeat music)

00:00:11.946 --> 00:00:13.560
(audience applauding)

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.960
Educators all over the
country had to get crafty

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:18.100
the moment schools closed their doors

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.860
and parents cried.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.030
Two teachers here in
Citrus Heights, California,

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:23.760
didn't just go viral,

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:24.790
this husband and wife pair

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:27.450
now stream a full
fledged production online

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:31.680
to keep their school's beloved
Friday Sing Show alive.

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:32.570
Oh, they're so cute.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:34.050
Not only do they sing,

00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:35.270
they do puppet shows,

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:36.930
guide kids through crafts

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:39.760
and pack in educational info between.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.040
I'm telling you, Mr. Fred Rogers
would be so proud of them.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.327
Let's get this cute couple
on the line right now.

00:00:44.327 --> 00:00:45.697
(audience applauding)

00:00:45.697 --> 00:00:47.120
Hi Joshua and Jennifer.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:49.686
(audience applauding)

00:00:49.686 --> 00:00:51.120
Oh, my God! I love y'all.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.520
So how did you come up with this, Joshua?

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:56.040
- Well, my wife and I
have been teaching here

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:59.010
at Orchard Elementary for many years

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:02.300
and she teaches third grade
and I teach fourth grade

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:06.240
and every Friday for the
past 20 years or more,

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:09.670
we've been hosting a live
assembly at our school

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:12.350
on Friday mornings for all of our students

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:14.950
and we sing there and gather together.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:16.730
But when the schools closed,

00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:18.970
of course we weren't
able to meet in person.

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:23.310
So we decided to take
the show to the internet.

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:25.980
And so even now that we're back at school,

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:28.190
it's something that we
find really important

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:31.130
and we want to continue
to share that with,

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:32.730
not just our Orchard community,

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:35.464
but our entire neighborhood and beyond.

00:01:35.464 --> 00:01:36.510
(audience applauding)

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:37.560
- Yeah!

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:39.500
Well, Jennifer, this started small,

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.800
but it's become quite a
big production, right?

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:44.720
- It sure did start small.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:47.250
We started out in our
garage, like he said,

00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:49.690
and recruited our own two children

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:53.520
to help us film using just
our smartphones at first.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:56.750
We, over time, you know,
made a lot of mistakes

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:58.880
and had a lot of laughs
through that process

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:01.370
and decided to just keep creating.

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:03.050
We wanted to

00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:04.860
add books and puppets

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:08.470
and we design all our own
sets and costumes, puppets,

00:02:08.470 --> 00:02:09.960
and just have so much fun.

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:14.010
It's been a lot of our weekend
time creating and rehearsing,

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:16.730
and it's just brought
our family so much joy

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:19.560
and the connections we've
made with the community,

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:20.830
you know, really keep us going.

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:23.930
And we're actually working
on our new series right now.

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:25.190
We have a three-part series

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:27.130
on friendship coming out very soon

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:29.540
and we are just super
excited to get it out

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:31.085
and to share it and-
- Ah!

00:02:31.085 --> 00:02:32.630
(audience applauding)

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:34.370
Well, thank you guys so much.

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:35.790
This is such a beautiful
thing you're doing

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:36.850
for not only your community,

00:02:36.850 --> 00:02:38.590
but the larger community now online.

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:41.553
I'm liking your posts
right now, all right.

00:02:41.553 --> 00:02:43.490
(Jennifer laughing)
- [Joshua] Yes!

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:44.480
- All right, that's not all.

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:46.810
Our season long partner, Pilot Pen,

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:48.670
the go-to pen of the
Kelly Clarkson Show likes

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:52.110
to celebrate those who create
fearlessly, just like you.

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:54.090
So they'll be using their
Frixion erasable pen

00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:55.970
to write you a check
for a thousand dollars.

00:02:55.970 --> 00:02:56.803
How's that sound?

00:02:56.803 --> 00:02:58.515
(audience cheering)

00:02:58.515 --> 00:03:00.886
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:00.886 --> 00:03:01.719
- Thank you-

00:03:01.719 --> 00:03:04.070
- [Kelly] You can get real
crafty with that kind of money.

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:05.107
I'm just saying.

